I just moved my boot disk from an old machine to a new machine.  The
new machine has AES-NI and it failed to boot.

The problem appears to be that aesni-intel, when loaded as a module,
makes cryptsetup fail on an aes-xts-plain drive.  The error looks
like:

device-mapper: reload ioctl failed: Invalid argument
device-mapper: table: 253:0: crypt: Error allocating crypto tfm
device-mapper: ioctl: error adding target to table

If I blacklist aesni-intel or compile it directly into the kernel,
everything works.  I have this problem on 2.6.38.5 and 2.6.39-rc6.

/proc/crypto with aesni-intel builtin and as a module attached.


I don't know enough about how cryptoapi works to really debug it, but
my .config for the modular case contains:

